export const ROOT_PORTFOLIO_README = "# Farjad Zeya \u2014 Data Analyst Portfolio\n**Email:** [farjadzeya1234@gmail.com](mailto:farjadzeya1234@gmail.com) | **Phone:** +91 6204812301 | **Location:** New Delhi, India  \n**Specialization:** Python (pandas, NumPy) \u2022 SQL (MySQL) \u2022 Microsoft Excel \u2022 Power BI \u2022 Business Intelligence \u2022 MIS Reporting\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc68\u200d\ud83d\udcbb Professional Summary\nResults-oriented Data Analyst with a B.Tech in Computer Science (Jamia Hamdard, 2026) and hands-on experience across the entire data lifecycle \u2014 data extraction, cleaning, exploratory data analysis (EDA), statistical evaluation, KPI dashboarding, and stakeholder reporting. Currently working as a **Maintenance Data Analyst at CK Infrastructure Ltd**, maintaining diesel consumption databases and delivering Excel/Pivot Table MIS reports to management. Previously completed a Data Analyst Internship at **Cochain LLC** conducting Python EDA and machine learning evaluation.\n\nThis portfolio repository houses **four production-quality, end-to-end data analytics projects** designed to solve mission-critical business problems across E-Commerce, Retail Banking, Supply Chain Logistics, and Digital Marketing.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Technical Skills Matrix\n\n| Category | Competencies & Tools |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Data Analysis & EDA** | Python (`pandas`, `NumPy`, `Matplotlib`), SQL, Exploratory Data Analysis, Descriptive Statistics, Trend Analysis, RFM Analysis, Churn & Funnel Analysis |\n| **Databases & Querying** | MySQL, Relational Database Design, Complex `JOIN`s, Subqueries, Common Table Expressions (CTEs), Window Functions (`NTILE`, `LAG`, `LEAD`, `DENSE_RANK`, `SUM OVER`) |\n| **Reporting & Dashboards** | Microsoft Power BI (Star Schema, DAX Calculated Measures, Time Intelligence, Slicers), Excel Pivot Tables & Charts, MIS Executive Reporting |\n| **Data Quality & Pipeline** | Data Cleaning, Missing Value Imputation, Deduplication, Data Integrity Enforcement, Feature Engineering, Outlier Treatment |\n| **Developer Tools** | Git, GitHub, VS Code, Jupyter Notebook, Streamlit, Linux CLI |\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcc2 Featured Portfolio Projects\n\n### [Project 1: E-Commerce Customer & Sales Analytics](./projects/01-ecommerce-customer-sales-analytics/)\n* **Technologies:** SQL (MySQL), Python (pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib), Power BI, Streamlit\n* **Core Objective:** Analyzed sales, profit margins, customer cohorts, product categories, and geographic regions to optimize pricing and discount governance.\n* **Key Technical Deliverables:**\n  - Ingested and cleaned ~2,100 multi-region raw transactions with missing discounts and anomalous formatting.\n  - Implemented **RFM (Recency, Frequency, Monetary) customer segmentation** using MySQL CTEs and Python quantiles.\n  - Built an interactive **Power BI KPI Dashboard** with dynamic DAX time-intelligence formulas (YoY, MoM growth).\n  - Proved Pareto 80/20 distribution: 38% of revenue generated by top 14% \"Champions\" cohort.\n* **Repository Link:** [View Project 1 Directory](./projects/01-ecommerce-customer-sales-analytics/)\n\n---\n\n### [Project 2: Banking Customer Churn & Retention Analysis](./projects/02-banking-customer-churn-retention/)\n* **Technologies:** SQL (MySQL), Python (pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib), Power BI, Streamlit\n* **Core Objective:** Measured customer attrition rate (20.4%) across 2,500 retail banking accounts and evaluated behavioral churn drivers to safeguard $48M+ in deposits.\n* **Key Technical Deliverables:**\n  - Evaluated multi-dimensional churn drivers across tenure cohorts, digital activity, and account balance brackets.\n  - Uncovered the **Multi-Product Paradox**: clients with 2 products achieve optimal retention (8.1% churn), whereas clients with 3-4 products experience >78% churn.\n  - Engineered a composite **Retention Risk Tier** model (\"High Risk\", \"Medium Risk\", \"Low Risk\") in Python & SQL.\n  - Created a Power BI Retention Cockpit prioritizing at-risk high-balance depositors for relationship management intervention.\n* **Repository Link:** [View Project 2 Directory](./projects/02-banking-customer-churn-retention/)\n\n---\n\n### [Project 3: Supply Chain & Delivery Performance Analytics](./projects/03-supply-chain-delivery-analytics/)\n* **Technologies:** SQL (MySQL), Microsoft Excel (Advanced Pivot Tables, MIS Reporting), Power BI\n* **Core Objective:** Analyzed on-time delivery (OTD %), dispatch delays, supplier reliability, and freight cost per KG across 2,200 consignments to identify fulfillment bottlenecks.\n* **Key Technical Deliverables:**\n  - Evaluated network-wide On-Time Delivery Rate (81.4%) and average delay durations (3.4 days).\n  - Built a comprehensive **Supplier Performance Scorecard** tracking OTD %, defect/damage frequency, and freight volume.\n  - Mapped a **Route Bottleneck Matrix** using SQL window functions (`DENSE_RANK()`), identifying severe dispatch latency at Kolkata Gateway Hub (WH-KOL-04).\n  - Designed an Excel MIS reporting model with dynamic `XLOOKUP`, `SUMIFS`, `AVERAGEIF`, and conditional formatting.\n* **Repository Link:** [View Project 3 Directory](./projects/03-supply-chain-delivery-analytics/)\n\n---\n\n### [Project 4: Marketing Campaign & Customer Conversion Analytics](./projects/04-marketing-campaign-conversion-analytics/)\n* **Technologies:** SQL (MySQL), Python (pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib), Power BI, Streamlit\n* **Core Objective:** Evaluated campaign ROI, Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC), and channel performance across 3,500 inbound leads and 10 digital campaigns.\n* **Key Technical Deliverables:**\n  - Mapped a full 6-stage **lead-to-customer conversion funnel** (Lead \u2794 MQL \u2794 SQL \u2794 Opportunity \u2794 Closed-Won) and pinpointed a 42% drop-off at the MQL-to-SQL handoff.\n  - Calculated channel-level unit economics: LinkedIn Ads delivered highest enterprise deal sizes ($24.5k) and 7.2x ROAS; Email delivered 1,240% net ROI; Influencer marketing proved unprofitable (0.82x ROAS).\n  - Designed interactive Power BI and Streamlit dashboards featuring conversion drop-off charts and budget allocation matrices.\n* **Repository Link:** [View Project 4 Directory](./projects/04-marketing-campaign-conversion-analytics/)\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\ude80 How to Set Up & Run Any Project Locally\n\nEach project is self-contained with its own datasets, scripts, SQL schemas, and interactive apps:\n\n```bash\n# Example: Running Project 1\ncd projects/01-ecommerce-customer-sales-analytics\n\n# 1. Set up a virtual environment\npython -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: .venv\\Scripts\\activate\n\n# 2. Install dependencies\npip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# 3. Execute the data cleaning and analysis pipeline\npython src/data_cleaning.py\npython src/analysis.py\n\n# 4. Launch the interactive dashboard\nstreamlit run streamlit_app.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcec Contact & Portfolio Inquiries\n- **Farjad Zeya**\n- **Email:** [farjadzeya1234@gmail.com](mailto:farjadzeya1234@gmail.com)\n- **Phone:** +91 6204812301\n- **Target Roles:** Data Analyst \u2022 MIS Analyst \u2022 Reporting Analyst \u2022 Business Intelligence Analyst\n";

